            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">A 45-year-old woman presented to the emergency department with ST-segment elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INVESTIGATION" NlmCategory="METHODS">Physical examination, electrocardiography, coronary angiography, echocardiography, cardiac computed tomography.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DIAGNOSIS" NlmCategory="METHODS">STEMI due to spontaneous left main coronary artery dissection involving left anterior descending, intermediate and left circumflex arteries.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="TREATMENT" NlmCategory="METHODS">Percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
